golem.wasm: the PDF of Golem as a WebAssembly reactor module
==============================================================

golem.wasm builds the PDF of a Golem project from the bytes of its files,
with the same build as `golem build --target pdf` of the native golem of
the same version, and reads no file. It is a WASI (preview 1) reactor
module: it imports only wasi_snapshot_preview1, and needs no preopened
directory. CI runs it under the node:wasi of Node, and every night under
Deno 2.9.8, under the C API of wasmtime 50.0.1 and, with
browser_wasi_shim 0.4.2, in Chromium (Chrome for Testing 157.0.8103.50) and
in the Safari of the macOS runner of GitHub Actions, and checks that each
gives the PDFs and the diagnostics of the native golem (docs/adr/0234,
docs/adr/0238). Deno runs the host of Node, scripts/wasm/run.mjs, as it is
(deno run --allow-read --allow-write): its node:wasi runs the module, so
no host of its own is needed. wasmtime runs it from a small C host,
scripts/wasm/run-wasmtime.c, as the CLI of wasmtime cannot write the input
into the memory of the module. The browsers run
scripts/wasm/browser/run.html.

The module uses the standard exception handling of WebAssembly (the form
with exnref: try_table, throw_ref), not the legacy one (try, catch,
delegate), so it needs a host that reads it: Chrome 137, Firefox 131,
Safari 18.4, Node 24.15, Deno 2.3.2, wasmtime 47 or later. It has
no plugins (golem-plugin): a project with [plugins] or a plugin filter in
[[filters]] gives the error G06106 and no PDF.

Exports
-------

The functions use the C ABI. The host calls _initialize once, then
hs_init(0, 0) once, then the others.

  uint8_t *golem_alloc(uint32_t len)
      a buffer of len bytes for the input
  void golem_free(uint8_t *p)
      frees a buffer of golem_alloc, golem_build_pdf or golem_version
  uint8_t *golem_build_pdf(const uint8_t *in, uint32_t len)
      reads the input frame, builds the PDF and returns the result frame
  uint32_t golem_result_len(const uint8_t *r)
      the length of a buffer of golem_build_pdf or golem_version
  uint8_t *golem_version(void)
      VERSION of Golem, in UTF-8 (its length is golem_result_len)

The module exports memory too, where the host writes the input and reads
the results.

The input frame
---------------

A sequence of files. Each file is the length of its path (uint32,
little-endian), its path (UTF-8), the length of its content (uint32,
little-endian) and its content. A path is relative to the root of the
project and normalised: no "." nor ".." segment, no empty segment, not
absolute, not a URL (manifest.toml, style.toml, chapter.gm,
fonts/NotoSerifJP-Regular.otf). No path comes twice. The files are those
of the project folder: manifest.toml, style.toml, the sources, the fonts,
the figures, the tables, the bibliographies and the .emet.

The result frame
----------------

One byte of status, the length of the PDF (uint32, little-endian), the
PDF, the length of the JSON of the diagnostics (uint32, little-endian) and
the JSON.

  status 0  built. A PDF of length 0: an error stopped it, and the JSON
            says why.
  status 1  the input frame cannot be read (a length beyond the end, a
            path that is not UTF-8 or not normalised, a path twice). Both
            lengths are 0.

The JSON is that of `golem build --target pdf --format json` on its
standard error: one object for each diagnostic, with the code, the
severity, the span (file, line, column) and the message. The build is that
of `golem build --target pdf` with its defaults: the profile dev, no crop
marks, the notices and the infos as by default.

